IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), PART XII -- Shareholders: requisition of a meeting,
-- meetings called by the court, disputes about elections, pooling and unanimous shareholder agreements
-- (ss 143 to 146).
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. The text this was encoded from is a plain-text rendering of the Department of Justice
-- Canada consolidation current to 2026-09-30 (last amended 2026-03-26); it is not an official version,
-- and nothing here has been verified against the official text. Contains information licensed under
-- the Open Government Licence - Canada.
--
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Rules are named `<what> within s N`. A court's order is the court's
-- discretion and is never decided: a rule here says who may apply, on what ground, and what power the court
-- has. The keel's input `there is a unanimous shareholder agreement` is answered by the s 146 rules here.
-- Dates: Part XII holds no enactment, assent or commencement provision, so no date is carried.

§ `Part XII -- Shareholders: requisition, court meetings, agreements (ss 143 to 146)`

§§ `s 143(1), (2) -- requisitioning a meeting`

-- (1) The holders of not less than five per cent of the issued shares that carry the right to vote at a meeting
-- sought to be held may requisition the directors to call a meeting for the purposes stated in the requisition.
-- The relation: the holders hold the power to requisition; the directors are under the liability. The fraction is
-- the shares the requisitioners hold of the issued shares carrying the right to vote at THAT meeting (the caller
-- divides); "not less than" makes exactly five per cent enough.
-- src:1773 | 143 (1) The holders of not less than five per cent of the issued shares of a corporation that carry the right to vote at a meeting sought to be held may requisition the directors to call a meeting of shareholders for the purposes stated in the requisition.
@ref CBCA s 143(1) (src:1773)
GIVEN `the fraction of the issued shares that carry the right to vote at the meeting sought to be held, held by the requisitioners` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`holders may requisition the directors to call a meeting within s 143(1)` MEANS
    `the fraction of the issued shares that carry the right to vote at the meeting sought to be held, held by the requisitioners` AT LEAST (5%)

-- (2) The requisition, which may consist of several documents of like form each signed by one or more
-- shareholders, shall state the business to be transacted and be sent to each director and to the registered
-- office of the corporation.
-- src:1775 | (2) The requisition referred to in subsection (1), which may consist of several documents of like form each signed by one or more shareholders, shall state the business to be transacted at the meeting and shall be sent to each director and to the registered office of the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 143(2) (src:1775)
GIVEN `the requisition states the business to be transacted at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requisition is sent to each director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requisition is sent to the registered office of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `if it consists of several documents, they are of like form and each is signed by one or more shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the requisition complies with s 143(2)` MEANS
        `the requisition states the business to be transacted at the meeting`
    AND `the requisition is sent to each director`
    AND `the requisition is sent to the registered office of the corporation`
    AND `if it consists of several documents, they are of like form and each is signed by one or more shareholders`

§§ `s 143(3) -- the directors call the meeting, unless`

-- On receiving the requisition the directors shall call a meeting to transact the stated business, unless (a) a
-- record date has been fixed under 134(1)(c) and notice of it has been given under 134(3); (b) the directors have
-- called a meeting and given notice under s 135; or (c) the business stated includes matters described in paragraphs
-- 137(5)(b) to (e). "(b) to (e)" takes in (b.1) by its place in the list (fork F-143-3c): the five matters are
-- one input, `matters described in s 137(5)(b) to (e)` (the proposals module's limbs (b), (b.1), (c), (d), (e)).
-- The relation: the requisitioners hold the claim; the directors owe the call.
-- src:1777 | (3) On receiving the requisition referred to in subsection (1), the directors shall call a meeting of shareholders to transact the business stated in the requisition, unless
-- src:1778 | (a) a record date has been fixed under paragraph 134(1)(c) and notice of it has been given under subsection 134(3);
-- src:1779 | (b) the directors have called a meeting of shareholders and have given notice thereof under section 135; or
-- src:1780 | (c) the business of the meeting as stated in the requisition includes matters described in paragraphs 137(5)(b) to (e).
@ref CBCA s 143(3) (src:1777-1780)
GIVEN `holders may requisition the directors to call a meeting within s 143(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requisition complies with s 143(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a record date has been fixed under paragraph 134(1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `notice of the record date has been given under subsection 134(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors have called a meeting of shareholders and have given notice of it under section 135` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the business stated in the requisition includes matters described in paragraphs 137(5)(b) to (e)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the directors must call the meeting within s 143(3)` MEANS
        `holders may requisition the directors to call a meeting within s 143(1)`
    AND `the requisition complies with s 143(2)`
    AND (NOT (    (    `a record date has been fixed under paragraph 134(1)(c)`
                   AND `notice of the record date has been given under subsection 134(3)`)
              OR  `the directors have called a meeting of shareholders and have given notice of it under section 135`
              OR  `the business stated in the requisition includes matters described in paragraphs 137(5)(b) to (e)`))

§§ `s 143(4) -- a shareholder calls the meeting`

-- (4) If the directors do not within twenty-one days after receiving the requisition call a meeting, any
-- shareholder who signed the requisition may call it. The day of receipt is day 0 and the twenty-first day after it
-- is in time (the keel's convention, fork F1). The power arises only after that last day has passed, and, read with
-- (3), only where the directors were required to call the meeting (fork F-143-4).
-- src:1782 | (4) If the directors do not within twenty-one days after receiving the requisition referred to in subsection (1) call a meeting, any shareholder who signed the requisition may call the meeting.
@ref CBCA s 143(4) (src:1782)
`the twenty-one days of s 143(4)` MEANS `Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 21, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`

@ref CBCA s 143(4) (src:1782)
GIVEN `the date the directors received the requisition` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for the directors to call the meeting within s 143(4)` MEANS
    `the last day of` `the twenty-one days of s 143(4)` `counted from` `the date the directors received the requisition`

@ref CBCA s 143(4) (src:1782)
GIVEN `the person signed the requisition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors were required to call the meeting by s 143(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the directors received the requisition` IS A DATE
      `the date the directors called a meeting, if they did` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date the shareholder calls the meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a shareholder who signed may call the meeting within s 143(4)` MEANS
        `the person signed the requisition`
    AND `the directors were required to call the meeting by s 143(3)`
    AND (NOT (CONSIDER `the date the directors called a meeting, if they did`
              WHEN JUST called THEN `done within the time limit` `the twenty-one days of s 143(4)` `the date the directors received the requisition` called
              WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE))
    AND `the date the shareholder calls the meeting` GREATER THAN (`the last day for the directors to call the meeting within s 143(4)` `the date the directors received the requisition`)

§§ `s 143(5), (6) -- procedure, and reimbursement`

-- (5) A meeting called under the section shall be called as nearly as possible in the manner in which meetings are to
-- be called pursuant to the by-laws, Part XII and Part XIII.
-- src:1784 | (5) A meeting called under this section shall be called as nearly as possible in the manner in which meetings are to be called pursuant to the by-laws, this Part and Part XIII.
@ref CBCA s 143(5) (src:1784)
GIVEN `the meeting is called under s 143` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is called as nearly as possible in the manner in which meetings are to be called pursuant to the by-laws, this Part and Part XIII` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the meeting is called as s 143(5) requires within s 143(5)` MEANS
        (NOT `the meeting is called under s 143`)
    OR  `it is called as nearly as possible in the manner in which meetings are to be called pursuant to the by-laws, this Part and Part XIII`

-- (6) Unless the shareholders otherwise resolve at a meeting called under (4), the corporation shall reimburse the
-- shareholders the expenses reasonably incurred by them in requisitioning, calling and holding the meeting. The duty is
-- read as arising on a requisition, and as open to a contrary resolution only at a meeting the shareholders called
-- under (4) (fork F-143-6). The relation: the shareholders hold the claim; the corporation owes the amount.
-- src:1786 | (6) Unless the shareholders otherwise resolve at a meeting called under subsection (4), the corporation shall reimburse the shareholders the expenses reasonably incurred by them in requisitioning, calling and holding the meeting.
@ref CBCA s 143(6) (src:1786)
GIVEN `a requisition was made under s 143(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the meeting was called by the shareholders under s 143(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shareholders resolved otherwise at that meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation must reimburse the shareholders' expenses within s 143(6)` MEANS
        `a requisition was made under s 143(1)`
    AND (NOT (    `the meeting was called by the shareholders under s 143(4)`
              AND `the shareholders resolved otherwise at that meeting`))

-- The amount is the expenses reasonably incurred, in dollars; where there is no duty the section gives no amount
-- (NOTHING).
@ref CBCA s 143(6) (src:1786)
GIVEN `the corporation must reimburse the shareholders' expenses within s 143(6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the expenses reasonably incurred by the shareholders in requisitioning, calling and holding the meeting, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the amount to reimburse within s 143(6)` MEANS
    IF `the corporation must reimburse the shareholders' expenses within s 143(6)`
    THEN JUST `the expenses reasonably incurred by the shareholders in requisitioning, calling and holding the meeting, in dollars`
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 144 -- a meeting called by the court`

-- (1) A court, on the application of a director, a shareholder entitled to vote at a meeting of shareholders, or the
-- Director, may order a meeting to be called, held and conducted in the manner the court directs, if (a) it is
-- impracticable to call the meeting within the time or in the manner required; (b) it is impracticable to conduct the
-- meeting in the manner required by the Act or the by-laws; or (c) the court thinks the meeting should be called, held
-- and conducted within the time or in the manner it directs for any other reason. The rule says who may apply, and
-- when the court's power arises; whether and how it orders is the court's.
-- src:1788 | 144 (1) A court, on the application of a director, a shareholder who is entitled to vote at a meeting of shareholders or the Director, may order a meeting of a corporation to be called, held and conducted in the manner that the court directs, if
-- src:1789 | (a) it is impracticable to call the meeting within the time or in the manner in which those meetings are to be called;
-- src:1790 | (b) it is impracticable to conduct the meeting in the manner required by this Act or the by-laws; or
-- src:1791 | (c) the court thinks that the meeting should be called, held and conducted within the time or in the manner it directs for any other reason.
@ref CBCA s 144(1) (src:1788-1791)
GIVEN `the applicant is a director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is a shareholder entitled to vote at a meeting of shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is the Director` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a person may apply to the court for a meeting within s 144(1)` MEANS
        `the applicant is a director`
    OR  `the applicant is a shareholder entitled to vote at a meeting of shareholders`
    OR  `the applicant is the Director`

@ref CBCA s 144(1) (src:1788-1791)
GIVEN `the application is made by a person who may apply` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is impracticable to call the meeting within the time or in the manner in which those meetings are to be called` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is impracticable to conduct the meeting in the manner required by this Act or the by-laws` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court thinks that the meeting should be called, held and conducted within the time or in the manner it directs for any other reason` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the court may order a meeting to be called, held and conducted within s 144(1)` MEANS
        `the application is made by a person who may apply`
    AND (    `it is impracticable to call the meeting within the time or in the manner in which those meetings are to be called`
         OR  `it is impracticable to conduct the meeting in the manner required by this Act or the by-laws`
         OR  `the court thinks that the meeting should be called, held and conducted within the time or in the manner it directs for any other reason`)

-- (2) Without restricting (1), the court may order that the quorum required by the by-laws or the Act be varied or
-- dispensed with at a meeting called, held and conducted pursuant to the section.
-- src:1793 | (2) Without restricting the generality of subsection (1), the court may order that the quorum required by the by-laws or this Act be varied or dispensed with at a meeting called, held and conducted pursuant to this section.
@ref CBCA s 144(2) (src:1793)
GIVEN `the meeting is called, held and conducted pursuant to s 144` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the court may vary or dispense with the quorum within s 144(2)` MEANS
    `the meeting is called, held and conducted pursuant to s 144`

-- (3) A meeting called, held and conducted pursuant to the section is for all purposes a meeting of shareholders duly
-- called, held and conducted.
-- src:1795 | (3) A meeting called, held and conducted pursuant to this section is for all purposes a meeting of shareholders of the corporation duly called, held and conducted.
@ref CBCA s 144(3) (src:1795)
GIVEN `the meeting is called, held and conducted pursuant to s 144` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the meeting is for all purposes a meeting duly called, held and conducted within s 144(3)` MEANS
    `the meeting is called, held and conducted pursuant to s 144`

§§ `s 145 -- court review of an election or appointment`

-- (1) A corporation, a shareholder or a director may apply to a court to determine any controversy with respect to an
-- election or appointment of a director or auditor of the corporation.
-- src:1797 | 145 (1) A corporation or a shareholder or director may apply to a court to determine any controversy with respect to an election or appointment of a director or auditor of the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 145(1) (src:1797)
GIVEN `the applicant is the corporation, a shareholder or a director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the controversy is with respect to an election or appointment of a director or auditor of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a person may apply to the court to determine a controversy within s 145(1)` MEANS
        `the applicant is the corporation, a shareholder or a director`
    AND `the controversy is with respect to an election or appointment of a director or auditor of the corporation`

-- (2) On an application under the section the court may make any order it thinks fit including, without limiting the
-- generality of that, orders of the four kinds listed, which are the constructors below. The rule says the court's power
-- to make an order of a kind arises on an application under the section; it does not say what order is made.
-- src:1799 | (2) On an application under this section, the court may make any order it thinks fit including, without limiting the generality of the foregoing,
-- src:1800 | (a) an order restraining a director or auditor whose election or appointment is challenged from acting pending determination of the dispute;
-- src:1801 | (b) an order declaring the result of the disputed election or appointment;
-- src:1802 | (c) an order requiring a new election or appointment, and including in the order directions for the management of the business and affairs of the corporation until a new election is held or appointment made; and
-- src:1803 | (d) an order determining the voting rights of shareholders and of persons claiming to own shares.
@ref CBCA s 145(2) (src:1799-1803)
DECLARE `Kind of order under s 145(2)` IS ONE OF
    `an order restraining a director or auditor whose election or appointment is challenged from acting pending determination of the dispute`
    `an order declaring the result of the disputed election or appointment`
    `an order requiring a new election or appointment, with directions for the management of the business and affairs of the corporation until it is held or made`
    `an order determining the voting rights of shareholders and of persons claiming to own shares`
    `any other order the court thinks fit`

@ref CBCA s 145(2) (src:1799-1803)
GIVEN `the application is made under s 145` IS A BOOLEAN
      kind IS A `Kind of order under s 145(2)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the court may make an order of a kind within s 145(2)` MEANS
    `the application is made under s 145`

§§ `s 145.1 -- pooling agreement`

-- A written agreement between two or more shareholders may provide that in exercising voting rights the shares held by
-- them shall be voted as provided in the agreement. The relation: the parties hold the power to bind their votes; each
-- bears the liability of being bound.
-- src:1805 | 145.1 A written agreement between two or more shareholders may provide that in exercising voting rights the shares held by them shall be voted as provided in the agreement.
@ref CBCA s 145.1 (src:1805)
GIVEN `the agreement is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of shareholders who are parties to the agreement` IS A NUMBER
      `the agreement provides how the shares held by them are to be voted in exercising voting rights` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an agreement may bind the shares to be voted as provided within s 145.1` MEANS
        `the agreement is in writing`
    AND `the number of shareholders who are parties to the agreement` AT LEAST 2
    AND `the agreement provides how the shares held by them are to be voted in exercising voting rights`

§§ `s 146 -- unanimous shareholder agreement`

-- (1) An otherwise lawful written agreement among all the shareholders, or among all the shareholders and one or more
-- persons who are not shareholders, that restricts in whole or in part the powers of the directors to manage, or supervise
-- the management of, the business and affairs of the corporation is valid. The relation: the parties hold the power to make
-- it; the directors bear the liability of the restriction.
-- src:1807 | 146 (1) An otherwise lawful written agreement among all the shareholders of a corporation, or among all the shareholders and one or more persons who are not shareholders, that restricts, in whole or in part, the powers of the directors to manage, or supervise the management of, the business and affairs of the corporation is valid.
@ref CBCA s 146(1) (src:1807)
GIVEN `the agreement is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement is otherwise lawful` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all the shareholders of the corporation are parties to the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement restricts, in whole or in part, the powers of the directors to manage, or supervise the management of, the business and affairs of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the agreement is valid within s 146(1)` MEANS
        `the agreement is in writing`
    AND `the agreement is otherwise lawful`
    AND `all the shareholders of the corporation are parties to the agreement`
    AND `the agreement restricts, in whole or in part, the powers of the directors to manage, or supervise the management of, the business and affairs of the corporation`

-- (2) If a person who is the beneficial owner of all the issued shares makes a written declaration that restricts in whole
-- or in part the powers of the directors, the declaration is deemed to be a unanimous shareholder agreement.
-- src:1809 | (2) If a person who is the beneficial owner of all the issued shares of a corporation makes a written declaration that restricts in whole or in part the powers of the directors to manage, or supervise the management of, the business and affairs of the corporation, the declaration is deemed to be a unanimous shareholder agreement.
@ref CBCA s 146(2) (src:1809)
GIVEN `the person is the beneficial owner of all the issued shares of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the declaration is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the declaration restricts, in whole or in part, the powers of the directors to manage, or supervise the management of, the business and affairs of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the declaration is deemed to be a unanimous shareholder agreement within s 146(2)` MEANS
        `the person is the beneficial owner of all the issued shares of the corporation`
    AND `the declaration is in writing`
    AND `the declaration restricts, in whole or in part, the powers of the directors to manage, or supervise the management of, the business and affairs of the corporation`

-- The keel's input `there is a unanimous shareholder agreement` is answered by this: a valid (1) agreement or a (2) declaration.
@ref CBCA s 146(1), (2) helper (src:1807 src:1809)
GIVEN `the agreement is valid within s 146(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the declaration is deemed to be a unanimous shareholder agreement within s 146(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`there is a unanimous shareholder agreement within s 146(1) and (2)` MEANS
        `the agreement is valid within s 146(1)`
    OR  `the declaration is deemed to be a unanimous shareholder agreement within s 146(2)`

-- (3) A purchaser or transferee of shares subject to a unanimous shareholder agreement is deemed to be a party to it.
-- src:1811 | (3) A purchaser or transferee of shares subject to a unanimous shareholder agreement is deemed to be a party to the agreement.
@ref CBCA s 146(3) (src:1811)
GIVEN `the person is a purchaser or transferee of shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares are subject to a unanimous shareholder agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the purchaser or transferee is deemed to be a party within s 146(3)` MEANS
        `the person is a purchaser or transferee of shares`
    AND `the shares are subject to a unanimous shareholder agreement`

-- (4) If notice of the existence of the agreement is not given to a purchaser or transferee, in the manner referred to in
-- s 49(8) or otherwise, the purchaser or transferee may, no later than 30 days after they become aware of the agreement,
-- rescind the transaction by which they acquired the shares. The day of awareness is day 0 and the thirtieth day after it
-- is in time (the keel's convention, fork F1). Section 49(8) is out of range.
-- src:1813 | (4) If notice is not given to a purchaser or transferee of the existence of a unanimous shareholder agreement, in the manner referred to in subsection 49(8) or otherwise, the purchaser or transferee may, no later than 30 days after they become aware of the existence of the unanimous shareholder agreement, rescind the transaction by which they acquired the shares.
@ref CBCA s 146(4) (src:1813)
`the thirty days of s 146(4)` MEANS `Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 30, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`

@ref CBCA s 146(4) (src:1813)
GIVEN `the date the purchaser or transferee became aware of the unanimous shareholder agreement` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to rescind within s 146(4)` MEANS
    `the last day of` `the thirty days of s 146(4)` `counted from` `the date the purchaser or transferee became aware of the unanimous shareholder agreement`

-- out of range: section 49(8) (piece for Part VI)
@ref CBCA s 146(4) (src:1813)
GIVEN `notice of the existence of the agreement was given to the purchaser or transferee, in the manner referred to in subsection 49(8) or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the purchaser or transferee became aware of the unanimous shareholder agreement` IS A DATE
      `the date the purchaser or transferee rescinds the transaction` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the purchaser or transferee may rescind the transaction within s 146(4)` MEANS
        (NOT `notice of the existence of the agreement was given to the purchaser or transferee, in the manner referred to in subsection 49(8) or otherwise`)
    AND `done within the time limit` `the thirty days of s 146(4)` `the date the purchaser or transferee became aware of the unanimous shareholder agreement` `the date the purchaser or transferee rescinds the transaction`

-- (5) To the extent that the agreement restricts the powers of the directors, the parties who are given that power to
-- manage or supervise have all the rights, powers, duties and liabilities of a director, whether under the Act or otherwise,
-- including any defences available to the directors; and the directors are relieved of theirs, including their liabilities
-- under s 119 (out of range: section 119), to the same extent. "To the extent" is the one input: is this right, power, duty or
-- liability one the agreement takes from the directors.
-- src:1815 | (5) To the extent that a unanimous shareholder agreement restricts the powers of the directors to manage, or supervise the management of, the business and affairs of the corporation, parties to the unanimous shareholder agreement who are given that power to manage or supervise the management of the business and affairs of the corporation have all the rights, powers, duties and liabilities of a director of the corporation, whether they arise under this Act or otherwise, including any defences available to the directors, and the directors are relieved of their rights, powers, duties and liabilities, including their liabilities under section 119, to the same extent.
@ref CBCA s 146(5) (src:1815)
GIVEN `the right, power, duty or liability is one the agreement takes from the directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a party to the agreement who is given the power to manage or supervise the management of the business and affairs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the party has the right, power, duty or liability of a director within s 146(5)` MEANS
        `the right, power, duty or liability is one the agreement takes from the directors`
    AND `the person is a party to the agreement who is given the power to manage or supervise the management of the business and affairs`

@ref CBCA s 146(5) (src:1815)
GIVEN `the right, power, duty or liability is one the agreement takes from the directors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the directors are relieved of the right, power, duty or liability within s 146(5)` MEANS
    `the right, power, duty or liability is one the agreement takes from the directors`

-- (6) Nothing in the section prevents shareholders from fettering their discretion when exercising the powers of directors
-- under a unanimous shareholder agreement.
-- src:1817 | (6) Nothing in this section prevents shareholders from fettering their discretion when exercising the powers of directors under a unanimous shareholder agreement.
@ref CBCA s 146(6) (src:1817)
GIVEN `the shareholders exercise the powers of directors under a unanimous shareholder agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`shareholders may fetter their discretion within s 146(6)` MEANS
    `the shareholders exercise the powers of directors under a unanimous shareholder agreement`
